---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../site/styles/field-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Field study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of form fields for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="field-study">
    <div class="shell field-study-intro">
      <a class="field-study-back" href="/prototypes/footer-study/">← Footer study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should a form invite a reply?</h1>
      <p class="field-study-lede">Three field treatments for the request path. Clear labels, easy scanning, and enough warmth to feel like a conversation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell field-study-grid">
      <article class="field-option"><p class="field-option-name"><span>A</span> Framed field</p><div class="field-demo field-demo--framed"><label for="a">Business name</label><input id="a" value="The Seaside Café" /></div><p>Current direction: a clear border and quiet radius create a familiar form control.</p></article>
      <article class="field-option"><p class="field-option-name"><span>B</span> Underline field</p><div class="field-demo field-demo--underline"><label for="b">Business name</label><input id="b" value="The Seaside Café" /></div><p>More editorial and lightweight. The field is defined by one rule beneath the text.</p></article>
      <article class="field-option"><p class="field-option-name"><span>C</span> Blue focus</p><div class="field-demo field-demo--focus"><label for="c">Business name</label><input id="c" value="The Seaside Café" /></div><p>Quiet at rest, then uses blue when active so the next action is unmistakable.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
